---Describes the managed cluster resource properties.
---@class azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterProperties
---@field dnsName string The cluster dns name.
---@field fqdn? string The fully qualified domain name associated with the public load balancer of the cluster.
---@field ipv4Address? string The IPv4 address associated with the public load balancer of the cluster.
---@field clusterId? string A service generated unique identifier for the cluster resource.
---@field clusterState? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ClusterState The current state of the cluster.
---@field clusterCertificateThumbprints? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesClusterCertificateThumbprintsList List of thumbprints of the cluster certificates.
---@field clientConnectionPort? number The port used for client connections to the cluster.
---@field httpGatewayConnectionPort? number The port used for HTTP connections to the cluster.
---@field adminUserName string VM admin user name.
---@field adminPassword? distilled.Secret VM admin user password.
---@field loadBalancingRules? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesLoadBalancingRulesList Load balancing rules that are applied to the public load balancer of the cluster.
---@field allowRdpAccess? boolean Setting this to true enables RDP access to the VM. The default NSG rule opens RDP port to Internet which can be overridden with custom Network Security Rules. The default value for this setting is false.
---@field networkSecurityRules? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesNetworkSecurityRulesList Custom Network Security Rules that are applied to the Virtual Network of the cluster.
---@field clients? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesClientsList Client certificates that are allowed to manage the cluster.
---@field azureActiveDirectory? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.AzureActiveDirectory The AAD authentication settings of the cluster.
---@field fabricSettings? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesFabricSettingsList The list of custom fabric settings to configure the cluster.
---@field provisioningState? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedResourceProvisioningState The provisioning state of the managed cluster resource.
---@field clusterCodeVersion? string The Service Fabric runtime version of the cluster. This property is required when **clusterUpgradeMode** is set to 'Manual'. To get list of available Service Fabric versions for new clusters use [ClusterVersion API](./ClusterVersion.md). To get the list of available version for existing clusters use **availableClusterVersions**.
---@field clusterUpgradeMode? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesClusterUpgradeMode The upgrade mode of the cluster when new Service Fabric runtime version is available.
---@field clusterUpgradeCadence? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ClusterUpgradeCadence Indicates when new cluster runtime version upgrades will be applied after they are released. By default is Wave0. Only applies when **clusterUpgradeMode** is set to 'Automatic'.
---@field addonFeatures? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesAddonFeaturesList List of add-on features to enable on the cluster.
---@field enableAutoOSUpgrade? boolean Enables automatic OS upgrade for node types created using OS images with version 'latest'. The default value for this setting is false.
---@field zonalResiliency? boolean Indicates if the cluster has zone resiliency.
---@field applicationTypeVersionsCleanupPolicy? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ApplicationTypeVersionsCleanupPolicy The policy used to clean up unused versions.
---@field enableIpv6? boolean Setting this to true creates IPv6 address space for the default VNet used by the cluster. This setting cannot be changed once the cluster is created. The default value for this setting is false.
---@field subnetId? string If specified, the node types for the cluster are created in this subnet instead of the default VNet. The **networkSecurityRules** specified for the cluster are also applied to this subnet. This setting cannot be changed once the cluster is created.
---@field ipTags? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesIpTagsList The list of IP tags associated with the default public IP address of the cluster.
---@field ipv6Address? string IPv6 address for the cluster if IPv6 is enabled.
---@field enableServicePublicIP? boolean Setting this to true will link the IPv4 address as the ServicePublicIP of the IPv6 address. It can only be set to True if IPv6 is enabled on the cluster.
---@field auxiliarySubnets? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesAuxiliarySubnetsList Auxiliary subnets for the cluster.
---@field serviceEndpoints? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ManagedClusterPropertiesServiceEndpointsList Service endpoints for subnets in the cluster.
---@field zonalUpdateMode? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ZonalUpdateMode Indicates the update mode for Cross Az clusters.
---@field useCustomVnet? boolean For new clusters, this parameter indicates that it uses Bring your own VNet, but the subnet is specified at node type level; and for such clusters, the subnetId property is required for node types.
---@field publicIPPrefixId? string Specify the resource id of a public IPv4 prefix that the load balancer will allocate a public IPv4 address from. This setting cannot be changed once the cluster is created.
---@field publicIPv6PrefixId? string Specify the resource id of a public IPv6 prefix that the load balancer will allocate a public IPv6 address from. This setting cannot be changed once the cluster is created.
---@field ddosProtectionPlanId? string Specify the resource id of a DDoS network protection plan that will be associated with the virtual network of the cluster.
---@field upgradeDescription? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.ClusterUpgradePolicy The policy to use when upgrading the cluster.
---@field httpGatewayTokenAuthConnectionPort? number The port used for token-auth based HTTPS connections to the cluster. Cannot be set to the same port as HttpGatewayEndpoint.
---@field enableHttpGatewayExclusiveAuthMode? boolean If true, token-based authentication is not allowed on the HttpGatewayEndpoint. This is required to support TLS versions 1.3 and above. If token-based authentication is used, HttpGatewayTokenAuthConnectionPort must be defined.
---@field autoGeneratedDomainNameLabelScope? azure.servicefabricmanagedclusters.AutoGeneratedDomainNameLabelScope This property is the entry point to using a public CA cert for your cluster cert. It specifies the level of reuse allowed for the custom FQDN created, matching the subject of the public CA cert.
---@field allocatedOutboundPorts? number The number of outbound ports allocated for SNAT for each node in the backend pool of the default load balancer. The default value is 0 which provides dynamic port allocation based on pool size.
---@field VMImage? string The VM image the node types are configured with. This property controls the Service Fabric component packages to be used for the cluster. Allowed values are: 'Windows'. The default value is 'Windows'.
---@field enableOutboundOnlyNodeTypes? boolean Enable the creation of node types with only outbound traffic enabled. If set, a separate load balancer backend pool will be created for node types with inbound traffic enabled. Can only be set at the time of cluster creation.
---@field skipManagedNsgAssignment? boolean Determines whether to skip the assignment of the managed network security group (SF-NSG) to the cluster subnet when using a bring-your-own virtual network (BYOVNET) configuration. The default value is false.

